One signed connection to the MFX Hub API.

Every request is signed with the tenant's Ed25519 key, afresh on every attempt. A read that is rate limited is tried again after the platform's own `Retry-After`. A write is never retried, because a retried write is a second order.

Every call returns a `CompletableFuture`; block on it with `join()` if you want to. A failure completes it exceptionally with an [MfxException](#errors.MfxException), which `join()` throws as the cause of a `CompletionException`.

```java
try (MfxClient client = MfxClient.builder(URI.create("https://api.dev.mfxhub.com/v1"), keyId,
        SigningKey.parse(privateKeyPem)).build()) {
    TenantTerminal terminal = client.terminals().get(terminalId).join();
}
```

The stream's ordering rules for an `account:` channel, applied to the events you hand it.

Not a subscriber: it holds no socket and asks for nothing. The caller drives the stream, which lets one connection follow several terminals. Not thread-safe: hand it the events of one stream in order.

```java
LiveAccount live = new LiveAccount(terminalId);
for (StreamEvent event : stream) {
    AccountView view = live.apply(event);
    if (view != null) draw(view); else if (live.behind()) stream.resume(...);
}
```
